[0.000, "o", "(B\u001b[m\u001b[31;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mStart is fixed. Rolling out the production configuration.\u001b[39m\u001b[26X\r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThree replicas, and /work doing a real query against RDS.\u001b[39m\u001b[26X\u001b[34;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1mapp change\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[1mHEALTHZ_MODE  local -> db\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[64X\r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAnd I made /healthz honest: it queries the database now, same as /work. A health\u001b[39m   \r\n        \u001b[37mcheck that checks nothing is not a health check.\u001b[39m\u001b[47X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mTouching liveness?\u001b[39m\u001b[65X\r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mWhy? It is green.\u001b[39m\u001b[66X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mIt goes to the database through the same pool as /work.\u001b[39m\u001b[28X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mPool of four, the query is trivial. Ship it.\u001b[39m\u001b[39X\u001b[42;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[1mwhat changes: 12-startup-probe.yaml -> 13-under-load.yaml\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[44X"]
