[0.001, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d  \u001b[32m+apiVersion: keda.sh/v1alpha1\u001b[39m\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[32m+kind: ScaledObject\u001b[39m\u001b[82X\r\n  \u001b[32m+metadata:\u001b[39m\u001b[91X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  name: worker\u001b[39m\u001b[86X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  namespace: demo\u001b[39m\u001b[83X\r\n  \u001b[32m+spec:\u001b[39m\u001b[95X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  scaleTargetRef:\u001b[39m\u001b[83X\r\n  \u001b[32m+    name: worker\u001b[39m\u001b[84X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  minReplicaCount: 0\u001b[39m\u001b[80X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  maxReplicaCount: 24\u001b[39m\u001b[79X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  pollingInterval: 5\u001b[39m\u001b[80X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  cooldownPeriod: 30\u001b[39m\u001b[80X\r\n  \u001b[32m+  triggers:\u001b[39m\u001b[89X\r\n  \u001b[32m+    - type: aws-sqs-queue\u001b[39m\u001b[75X\r\n  \u001b[32m+      authenticationRef:\u001b[39m\u001b[76X\r\n  \u001b[32m+        name: sqs\u001b[39m\u001b[83X\r\n  \u001b[32m+      metadata:\u001b[39m\u001b[85X\r\n  \u001b[32m+        queueURL: ${QUEUE_URL}\u001b[39m\u001b[70X\r\n  \u001b[32m+        queueLength: \"20\"\u001b[39m\u001b[75X\r\n  \u001b[32m+        awsRegion: ${AWS_REGION}\u001b[39m\u001b[68X\r\n  \u001b[32m+        scaleOnInFlight: \"true\"\u001b[39m\u001b[69X\u001b[23;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m$ envsubst < k8s/incident2/20-ready-db-each-call.yaml | kubectl apply -f -\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[27X\r\n  deployment.apps/svc configured\u001b[71X\r\n  deployment.apps/wor"]
[0.000, "o", "ker created\u001b[71X\r\n  triggerauthentication.keda.sh/sqs created\u001b[60X\r\n  scaledobject.keda.sh/worker created\u001b[66X\u001b[29;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[37mShe said it out loud three times in the first incident. This time she writes it down.\u001b[39m\u001b[16X\u001b[31;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina's notes\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1m. HOW A READINESS FAILURE ACTUALLY REMOVES A POD\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[32X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m The Service does not route to pods. It routes to an EndpointSlice,\u001b[33X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m and readiness is what puts an address in it or takes it out.\u001b[39X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m One pod NotReady   -> its address is removed, the rest carry the load.\u001b[29X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Every pod NotReady -> the slice is empty and the Service has nowhere\u001b[31X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[23X\u001b[23Cto send anything. No error, no traffic, no pods.\u001b[29X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m So the blast radius of a readiness probe is not one replica.\u001b[39X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m It is every replica that shares whatever the probe is asking about.\u001b[32X\u001b[42;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[?2026l"]
