[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[35m\u001b[1m\r\n=======================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[35m\u001b[1m\r\n  2.2 . Black Friday: the queue fills\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[66X\u001b[35m\u001b[1m\r\n=======================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[6;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[37mBlack Friday. The work arrives as a queue, which is what the whole system was built for.\u001b[39m\u001b[13X\u001b[8;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m$ kubectl -n demo get scaledobject worker -o\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[57X\r\n    \u001b[36m\u001b[1mcustom-columns='NAME:.metadata.name,MIN:.spec.minReplicaCount,MAX:.spec.maxReplicaCount,TRIGGER:.sp\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[36m\u001b[1m\r\nec.triggers[*].type'\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[83X\r\n  NAME     MIN   MAX   TRIGGER\u001b[73X\r\n  worker   0     24    aws-sqs-queue\u001b[67X\u001b[14;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[37mKEDA watches the queue. Zero workers right now, because there is nothing to do.\u001b[39m\u001b[22X\u001b[16;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1mload starts\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[1mincident2-before\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m. enqueue . 20 rps for 90s\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[45X\r\n  \u001b[2mwatch the LOAD panel, bott"]
[0.000, "o", "om right\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[67X\r\n  \u001b[37mFilling the queue: two thousand messages a second going in.\u001b[39m\u001b[42X\u001b[20;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[1mKEDA, AND WHAT IT IS COUNTING\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m pollingInterval 5   it asks SQS how deep the queue is\u001b[46X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m queueLength 20      messages per worker it is willing to tolerate\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m maxReplicaCount 24  the ceiling, and the only thing stopping it\u001b[36X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m desired workers = queue depth / 20, capped at 24.\u001b[50X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m minReplicaCount is 0, so this scales up from nothing at all.\u001b[39X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Nothing in that formula knows why the queue is deep. A queue that\u001b[34X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m grows because the workers are stuck looks exactly like a queue that\u001b[32X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m grows because there is a lot of work.\u001b[62X\u001b[32;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m+ first workers scheduled (3s)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[71X\r\n  \u001b[31m\u001b[1m[>_<] KEDA     \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mQueue is deep. Adding workers.\u001b[39m\u001b[53X\r\n  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m[$_$] Karpenter\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2"]
[0.000, "o", "m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mPods are Pending. Buying machines.\u001b[39m\u001b[49X\u001b[36;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[2mqueue depth up, workers up, nodes up\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[65X\r\n  \u001b[2mqueue \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m1450/0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . workers \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m1/4\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . nodes \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m1\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m ~$0.02/h\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[56X\r\n  \u001b[1m 74s\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m███\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[2mlet it run . [->] skips\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[18X\r\n  worker-6bc9c889dd-cn4h2        \u001b[32m\u001b[1m1/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  Running\u001b[10X\u001b[10CR:0\u001b[45X\r\n  worker-6bc9c889dd-jdxtr        \u001b[31m\u001b[1m0/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  Running\u001b[10X\u001b[10CR:0\u001b[45X\r\n  worker-6bc9c889dd-k67rm        \u001b[31m\u001b[1m0/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  Running\u001b[10X\u001b[10CR:0\u001b[45X\r\n  worker-6bc9c889dd-xq8dg        \u001b[31m\u001b[1m0/1\u001b(B\u001b[m  Running\u001b[10X\u001b[10CR:0\u001b[45X\u001b[44;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[?2026l"]
