[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m probe asks the DB  ->  replicas NotReady  ->  workers stop consuming\u001b[31X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m   ^\u001b[53X\u001b[53C|\u001b[42X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m   |\u001b[53X\u001b[53Cv\u001b[42X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m  more nodes bought  <-  KEDA adds workers  <-  queue depth grows\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Every turn adds connections to the database that is already the\u001b[36X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m bottleneck, which makes the next turn worse. Nothing in the loop\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m is broken. Every component is doing exactly what it was asked.\u001b[37X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m The only part of it with a price tag is the bottom left.\u001b[43X\u001b[12;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[2mthroughput at zero, nodes still climbing\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[61X\r\n  \u001b[2mqueue \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m118979/301\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . workers \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m0/24\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m . nodes \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1m4\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m ~$0.07/h\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[51X\r\n  \u001b[1m  5s\u001b(B\u001b[m  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m█████████████████████████████████████████████████\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m"]
