[0.000, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d  \u001b[36m\u001b[1m$ kubectl -n demo get endpointslices -l kubernetes.io/service-name=svc -o\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[28X\r\n    \u001b[36m\u001b[1mcustom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,READY:.endpoints[*].conditions.ready\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[28X\r\n  NAME        READY\u001b[84X\r\n  svc-vf7jr   false,false,false\u001b[72X\r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mNo endpoints left in the Service. Not one.\u001b[39m\u001b[41X\u001b[7;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1mload stops\u001b(B\u001b[m   \u001b[1mincident2-before\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m. the panel keeps the summary\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[42X\u001b[9;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n=======================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n  Scaling did not save the service. Scaling is what took it down, and it bought hardware to do it.\u001b(B\u001b[m     \u001b[31m\u001b[1m\r\n=======================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[13;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[33m\u001b[1m\r\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[33m\u001b[1m\r\n  EVERYONE"]
[0.000, "o", " VOTE: what do you do first?\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[65X\u001b[33m\u001b[1m\r\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1m1\u001b(B\u001b[m . raise maxReplicaCount -- there are clearly not enough workers\u001b[36X\r\n  \u001b[1m2\u001b(B\u001b[m . restart the database -- it is slow\u001b[63X\r\n  \u001b[1m3\u001b(B\u001b[m . raise timeoutSeconds on the probe -- let it wait\u001b[49X\u001b[21;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[1m-> step 2.4: Madina unhooks the probe\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[64X\u001b[24;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[35m\u001b[1m\r\n=======================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[35m\u001b[1m\r\n  2.4 . Madina unhooks the probe\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[71X\u001b[35m\u001b[1m\r\n=======================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[28;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n  THE ANSWER: none of the three.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[71X\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------"]
[0.000, "o", "----------------------------------\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[33;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[37mAll three add work to the database, and the database is where everyone is already stuck. The first\u001b[39m   \r\n  \u001b[37mone also buys more machines.\u001b[39m\u001b[73X\u001b[36;103H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mUnhook the probe from the database.\u001b[39m\u001b[48X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mA background goroutine does SELECT 1 every two seconds with a timeout and stores\u001b[39m   \r\n        \u001b[37mthe result in a flag.\u001b[39m\u001b[74X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThe probe reads the flag. That is all.\u001b[39m\u001b[45X\r\n  \u001b[34m\u001b[1m(o_o) Timur    \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAnd if the database really does go down?\u001b[39m\u001b[43X\r\n  \u001b[32m\u001b[1m(^_^) Madina   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mThe flag goes stale and the pod honestly leaves the load balancer.\u001b[39m\u001b[17X\r\n  \u001b[33m\u001b[1m(-_-) Ruslan   \u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[2m>\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[37mAll twenty-four at once?\u001b[39m\u001b[59X\u001b[44;103H\u001b[1K\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[?2026l"]
